  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef wants to write a program to find the roots of a given quadratic equation using the formula method.\nYou are given the coefficients `a`, `b`, and `c`. Your task is to write a program to calculate and print the roots of the equation based on the discriminant.\n\nIf real and distinct, print:\n`Root1 = &lt;value&gt;`\n`Root2 = &lt;value&gt;`\nIf real and equal, print:\n`Root1 = Root2 = &lt;value&gt;`\nIf complex, print:\n`Root1 = &lt;realPart&gt; + i&lt;imaginaryPart&gt;`\n`Root2 = &lt;realPart&gt; - i&lt;imaginaryPart&gt;`\n\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThree space-separated float values `a`, `b`, and `c`.\n\n\nOutput Format\n\nPrint the roots in the given format.\nAll real values should be printed with 2 decimal places.",
